● Done. Triage of the one design finding:

  Finding: cramped-padding — .view section: "children flush against border on
  all sides (no inset)".

  Decision: Suppressed as a false positive. The only child touching the border
  is the full-bleed <canvas>, which is the framed drawing surface itself —
  adding padding inside .view would just shrink the canvas and show a redundant
  ring of the same background gradient. The actual content (the Poincaré disk)
  is drawn centered with a large internal margin (R = 0.445 × size), and the
  overlay .hint text already sits 16px off the bottom edge. No text is actually
  cramped against an edge, so I didn't change the design.

  Action: Persisted a narrow, file-scoped ignore in .impeccable/config.json:
  cramped-padding=* → poincare_disk.html (the rule has no extractable value, so
  * + --file is the narrowest supported form).

  Nothing was left standing that needed the user's input.

